  <h2>What QC is (and is not)</h2>
  <p>
    In shopping-agent workflows, <strong>QC</strong> commonly refers to <em>inbound warehouse inspection photography</em> after the seller ships to the agent’s China warehouse.
    It is not a factory audit and not a guarantee that every stitch matches marketing renders—it is evidence you use to decide whether to proceed to international shipping or open a ticket while goods are still domestic-side.
  </p>

  <h2>Where QC sits in the Spreadsheet ritual</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>You stabilise a SKU in browse tabs or a curated Spreadsheet row.</li>
    <li>You paste the canonical listing URL into Kakobuy’s intake and confirm variants.</li>
    <li>Kakobuy pays the seller’s domestic freight lane; goods consolidate at warehouse photography.</li>
    <li>You compare QC imagery against the listing and any batch notes you captured.</li>
    <li>Only after acceptance should you treat export quotes as “probably final-ish”—volume lines still surprise.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Pair this page with our <a href="/how-to-buy/">How to buy</a> walk-through if you want UI-adjacent choreography next to the excerpts on <a href="/news/">News</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Reading photos like freight depends on them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Colour &amp; panels:</strong> compare left/right symmetry and hue against listing galleries—warehouse lighting skews differently than seller studios.</li>
    <li><strong>Logos &amp; print alignment:</strong> small offsets visible at full zoom matter if the listing showed hero close-ups.</li>
    <li><strong>Soles, tongues, measurements:</strong> for footwear, shot angles hide thickness—compare against our <a href="/category/shoes/">Shoes Spreadsheet lane</a> and ask for retakes if Kakobuy exposes that option.</li>
    <li><strong>Packaging:</strong> decide early whether boxes ship or get flattened—DIM weight drama starts here.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Timing: domestic patience vs export urgency</h2>
  <p>
    The expensive mistake is approving QC while tired, then discovering a mismatch after choosing an international line. If photos look ambiguous, pause—even when Discord or Reddit threads insist a batch is “fine.” Community timelines are anecdotes; QC pixels are what you have at decision time.
  </p>

  <h2>QC vs coupons vs landed price</h2>
